WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:08.639 align:start position:19%
More than 12,000 strangers have reported
the exact same shadow figure. They live

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:14.000 align:start position:19%
on different continents. They speak
different languages. They have never

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:20.560 align:start position:19%
met. Every single one describes a tall
man wearing a wide-brimmed hat. Not a

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:26.000 align:start position:19%
demon with horns, not a ghost in white,
a man with a hat. The reports come from

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:32.079 align:start position:19%
forums, sleep clinics, and late night
radio callers. They span 40 years. They

00:00:29.679 --> 00:00:38.719 align:start position:19%
span the entire planet and the
description never changes.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:44.879 align:start position:19%
They call him the hatman. He shows up in
bedrooms at night. He stands in

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:49.520 align:start position:19%
doorways. He watches people sleep.
Sometimes he leans against a wall.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:54.160 align:start position:19%
Sometimes he sits at the foot of the
bed. And here is what makes him

00:00:52.079 --> 00:01:01.120 align:start position:19%
different from every other ghost story
ever told. Most ghosts haunt one house.

00:00:58.719 --> 00:01:07.920 align:start position:19%
This one haunts the entire human
species. He does not belong to one

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:14.720 align:start position:19%
family, one town, or one legend. He
belongs to everyone, everywhere, all at

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:20.880 align:start position:19%
once. Thousands of people describe him
the same way. 6 ft tall or more, black

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:26.960 align:start position:19%
from head to toe, darker than the
darkness around him. A wide-brimmed hat

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:32.960 align:start position:19%
like something from the 1800s. A long
coat that reaches his knees. He never

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:40.720 align:start position:19%
speaks, he never moves fast. He never
attacks, but he follows around. Everyone

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:47.360 align:start position:19%
can see him, but he never attacks, but
he follows around. Everyone can see him,

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:54.799 align:start position:19%
but he never attacks. But he never
attacks. But he never attacks. But he

00:01:51.040 --> 00:02:01.280 align:start position:19%
never attacks. But he never attacks. But
he never attacks. But he never attacks.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:08.640 align:start position:19%
But he never attacks. But he never
attacks. But he never attacks. But he

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:15.200 align:start position:19%
never attacks. But he never attacks. But
he never attacks. But he never attacks.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:22.239 align:start position:19%
But he never attacks. But he never
attacks. But he never attacks. But he

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:27.920 align:start position:19%
never attacks. But he never attacks. But
he never attacks. But he never attacks.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:34.959 align:start position:19%
But he never attack. But he never
attacks. But he never attacks. But he

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:41.120 align:start position:19%
never attacks. But he never attacks. But
he never attacks. But he never attacks.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:47.440 align:start position:19%
But he never attacks. But he never
attacks for minutes. Sometimes for what

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:52.239 align:start position:19%
feels like hours. Witnesses say the
worst part is not fear. It is the

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:56.720 align:start position:19%
feeling of being studied. Like he is
waiting for something only he

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:02.720 align:start position:19%
understands. Most encounters happen
during sleep paralysis. You wake up but

00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:07.599 align:start position:19%
your body refuses to move. You cannot
scream. You cannot run. Your brain is

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:12.720 align:start position:19%
fully alert. Your muscles are still
asleep. Scientists call it a glitch

00:03:10.159 --> 00:03:19.040 align:start position:19%
between dreaming and waking. Your mind
is on, your body is off. And in that

00:03:15.519 --> 00:03:24.879 align:start position:19%
trapped, helpless moment, he appears.
Usually in the corner, sometimes in the

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:29.599 align:start position:19%
doorway, always watching. Your heart
pounds so hard you are sure it will

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:34.000 align:start position:19%
burst. And he does not move a single
inch.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:38.560 align:start position:19%
Skeptics say it is all brain chemistry.
A stressed, exhausted brain, they argue,

00:03:36.799 --> 00:03:44.080 align:start position:19%
fills the darkness with a familiar
shape. Sleep paralysis hallucinations

00:03:41.599 --> 00:03:49.760 align:start position:19%
are common, they say. Millions of people
get them. The brain panics. It invents a

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:55.920 align:start position:19%
threat. It projects a figure into the
room. Nothing supernatural.

00:03:52.799 --> 00:04:03.519 align:start position:19%
Nothing real, just neurons misfiring in
the dark. It sounds reasonable. It

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:08.000 align:start position:19%
sounds scientific. It sounds comforting.
There is only one problem with it. Brain

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:13.200 align:start position:19%
chemistry should produce random
hallucinations, spiders crawling on the

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:18.720 align:start position:19%
ceiling, demons with red eyes, the
feeling of falling, your own worst fears

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:22.720 align:start position:19%
pulled straight from your own memories.
A scared child in Japan should see

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:28.880 align:start position:19%
something different from a scared adult
in Brazil. Different cultures, different

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:33.919 align:start position:19%
fears, different monsters. So why do
thousands of unconnected people

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:41.840 align:start position:19%
hallucinate the exact same man? Same
height, same hat, same coat,

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:46.320 align:start position:19%
say same stillness. Random chemistry
does not draw the same portrait 12,000

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:50.960 align:start position:19%
times.
Researchers who study sleep paralysis

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:55.280 align:start position:19%
have documented the pattern for decades.
They interview patients in sleep clinics

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:59.919 align:start position:19%
across the world. The details stay
eerily consistent across cultures that

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:08.639 align:start position:19%
have no contact with each other. A tall
figure, a hat, a coat, standing,

00:05:04.639 --> 00:05:13.759 align:start position:19%
watching, waiting. Some researchers call
it a cultural archetype, an image passed

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:18.560 align:start position:19%
through movies and stories. But the
reports predate the internet. They

00:05:15.919 --> 00:05:22.880 align:start position:19%
predate the movies. Some of the oldest
accounts come from people who had never

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:27.440 align:start position:19%
heard of him at all. And then there are
the cases that break the pattern

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:34.160 align:start position:19%
entirely because some witnesses were
never asleep at all. Not paralyzed, not

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:38.720 align:start position:19%
dreaming, wide awake, on their feet in
the middle of their normal lives. These

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:44.960 align:start position:19%
are the cases that skeptics cannot
explain away with brain chemistry. Case

00:05:41.919 --> 00:05:50.080 align:start position:19%
one, a truck driver in Texas. It
happened on a lonely stretch of highway

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:55.759 align:start position:19%
long after midnight. He had pulled over
at a rest stop at 2:00 in the morning,

00:05:52.240 --> 00:06:01.199 align:start position:19%
wide awake, drinking coffee. 17 years on
the road. He had seen everything.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:06.160 align:start position:19%
Nothing scared him anymore. He stepped
out of the cab to stretch his legs and

00:06:03.039 --> 00:06:11.199 align:start position:19%
clear his head. That is when he saw him.
A man in a long coat and a wide-brimmed

00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:17.039 align:start position:19%
hat standing between the parked trucks,
staring straight at him, not moving, not

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:22.160 align:start position:19%
blinking, just staring from about 30 ft
away. the driver shouted. He yelled for

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:27.840 align:start position:19%
the man to get away from the trucks. The
figure did not react, did not flinch,

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:33.199 align:start position:19%
did not turn. The driver took one step
forward, coffee still in his hand, and

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:39.199 align:start position:19%
the figure was simply gone, vanished
between one blink and the next. No

00:06:35.759 --> 00:06:44.240 align:start position:19%
footsteps, no car pulling away, no sound
at all. Just empty asphalt where a man

00:06:41.759 --> 00:06:49.680 align:start position:19%
had been standing. The driver got back
in his cab, locked the doors, and did

00:06:47.199 --> 00:06:55.440 align:start position:19%
not sleep that night. He quit night
routes 2 months later.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:07:00.560 align:start position:19%
Case two, a nurse in Ohio. She was
midshift, fully awake, checking on her

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:06.319 align:start position:19%
patients at 3:00 a.m. 12 years in the
ICU. She did not believe in ghosts. She

00:07:03.759 --> 00:07:12.000 align:start position:19%
believed in medicine. The heart monitor
in room 4 started beeping, an irregular

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:17.120 align:start position:19%
rhythm. She walked over calm and
professional and turned around to check

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:22.479 align:start position:19%
the screen. A tall man in a wide-brimmed
hat stood in the doorway of room 4. He

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:28.960 align:start position:19%
between her and the exit, watching the
patient, watching her. She froze. Her

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:34.479 align:start position:19%
training told her to speak, to ask who
he was, how he got in. She opened her

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:40.479 align:start position:19%
mouth. No sound came out. She blinked
hard once and he was gone. The doorway

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:45.599 align:start position:19%
was empty. The corridor beyond it was
empty. The patient in the bed never woke

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:50.080 align:start position:19%
up. The monitor showed nothing wrong.
She searched the floor. She checked the

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:54.720 align:start position:19%
security cameras. The camera showed her
standing alone in an empty corridor,

00:07:52.240 --> 00:08:00.319 align:start position:19%
staring at nothing. She never told her
family. She told her supervisor. It was

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:05.680 align:start position:19%
logged. And here is the part that should
chill you. Her supervisor pulled the

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:11.440 align:start position:19%
incident logs. Two other nurses had
filed reports that same month. Different

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:17.840 align:start position:19%
shifts, different nights. They had never
spoken to each other about it. All three

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:23.440 align:start position:19%
described the same figure. Tall hat,
coat, standing in a doorway, gone in a

00:08:21.039 --> 00:08:28.479 align:start position:19%
blink. None of them had ever heard of
the hatman. None of them knew the

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:33.039 align:start position:19%
stories. The hospital quietly moved all
three nurses to dayshifts. The reports

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:36.399 align:start position:19%
were filed away and never discussed
again.

00:08:34.479 --> 00:08:41.599 align:start position:19%
Case three is the one researchers
quietly discuss among themselves. A man

00:08:39.279 --> 00:08:50.480 align:start position:19%
in another country who had never heard
the stories described him perfectly.

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:56.240 align:start position:19%
Hat, coat, height, the watching, the
stillness. Every detail matched. A

00:08:54.240 --> 00:09:03.839 align:start position:19%
researcher asked him to draw the figure
from memory. He sketched it in under a

00:08:58.959 --> 00:09:09.360 align:start position:19%
minute. tall man, wide-brimmed hat, long
coat. Then the researcher showed him 20

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:15.839 align:start position:19%
other sketches drawn by strangers on
other continents. He went pale. They

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:21.600 align:start position:19%
were identical to his. He had never seen
the internet forums. He had never read a

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:25.600 align:start position:19%
single account. He drew the same man
anyway.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:31.440 align:start position:19%
So what is he? A glitch in the sleeping
brain? A shared nightmare passed quietly

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:36.080 align:start position:19%
through culture or something that
learned a long time ago that the edge of

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:42.560 align:start position:19%
sleep is the easiest door to walk
through. The skeptics have their answer.

00:09:39.279 --> 00:09:48.000 align:start position:19%
The witnesses have theirs. But 12,000
strangers cannot all be wrong about the

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:52.880 align:start position:19%
same hat. Tonight, when you wake up at
3:00 a.m. and cannot move, check the

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:56.880 align:start position:19%
corner of your room. And if he is
already looking back at you, do not

00:09:55.440 --> 00:10:02.720 align:start position:19%
scream.
He likes that.

